0.25 w BT/F4 10 Tf0 Tc 0 Tw 319.127 131.75 TD (vii)Tj/F7 24 Tf-157.002 491.25 TD (Preface)Tj/F7 14 Tf-18 -45.25 TD (1. About This Document)Tj/F6 10 Tf18 -21.5 TD (This user guide is designed to be used as a reference in your everyday use of )Tj0 -12 TD -0.264 Tw (PDQUEST\252. It provides detailed information about the tools and commands )TjT* 0 Tw (of PDQUEST for the Windows 95/98/NT 4.0 platforms.)Tj0 -20 TD (This guide assumes you have a working knowledge of your Windows )Tj0 -12 TD (operating system and its conventions, including how to use a mouse and )TjT* (standard menus and commands, and how to open, save, and close \336les. For )TjT* -0.395 Tw (help with any of these techniques, see the documentation that came with your )TjT* 0 Tw (computer.)Tj0 -20 TD (This guide uses certain text conventions to describe speci\336c commands and )Tj0 -12 TD (functions.)Tj/F7 14 Tf-18 -222.5 TD (2. Bio-Rad Listens)Tj/F6 10 Tf18 -21.5 TD (The staff at Bio-Rad are receptive to your suggestions. Many of the new )Tj0 -12 TD (features and enhancements in this version of PDQUEST are a direct result of )Tj/F5 10 Tf6 228 TD (Example)Tj108 0 TD (Indicates)Tj/F6 10 Tf-108 -20 TD (File > Open)Tj108 0 TD (Choosing the Open command under the File )Tj0 -12 TD (menu.)Tj-108 -20 TD (Dragging)Tj108 0 TD (Positioning the cursor on an object and holding )Tj0 -12 TD (down the left mouse button while you move the )TjT* (mouse.)Tj-108 -20 TD (Control+s)Tj108 0 TD (Holding down the Control key while typing the )Tj0 -12 TD (letter )Tj/F9 10 Tf25.449 0 TD (s)Tj/F6 10 Tf3.889 0 TD (.)Tj-137.338 -20 TD (Right-click/)Tj0 -12 TD (Left-click/)TjT* (Double-click)Tj108 24 TD (Clicking the right mouse button/)Tj0 -12 TD (Clicking the left mouse button/)TjT* (Clicking the left mouse button twice.)TjET161.75 245.25 0.5 171.5 ref 269.75 244.75 0.5 172.5 ref 503.75 245.25 0.5 171.5 ref 161.75 416.75 342.5 0.5 ref 161.75 396.75 342.5 0.5 ref 161.75 364.75