0.5 w BT/F4 12 Tf0 Tc 0 Tw 377.661 662.5 TD [ (Appendix I. T)74 (echniques)] TJ/F4 10 Tf-59.369 -530.75 TD (I-3)Tj/F7 11 Tf-165.167 500 TD (Calculate a curve which maps density to counts)Tj/F6 10 Tf9 -20.5 TD 2.704 Tw (The lowest point of the curve relates background density to 0.0 counts.)Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (Background is obtained from the calstrip scan by \336nding the mode of density)TjT* (values which are below the mean of all density values.)Tj0 -20 TD 0.175 Tw (A linear interpolation is performed between adjacent sample points to obtain)Tj0 -12 TD 1.435 Tw (values there. If the density value of any segment is within 1% of 255, it is)TjT* 2.463 Tw (considered saturated. The highest two nonsaturated samples are used to)TjT* 1.705 Tw (extrapolate the curve to saturation. This establishes the effective counts at)TjT* 0 Tw (saturation.)Tj0 -20 TD (If the slope of a curve segment falls below 10% of the highest value ever seen,)Tj0 -12 TD 2.898 Tw (saturation is set at the sample point at the lower end of the offending)TjT* 1.436 Tw (segment. This is only necessary when the \336lm response decreases below 2)TjT* 1.653 Tw (O.D. This normally indicates a failure of \336lm processing. The user should)TjT* 4.427 Tw (diagnose the problem in the \336lm exposure/development process and)TjT* 2.384 Tw (reprocess the gel if possible. The linearity of the \336lm response has been)TjT* 0 Tw (compromised.)Tj/F7 11 Tf-9 -27.5 TD [ (T)36 (ranslate the 2-D scan)] TJ/F6 10 Tf9 -20.5 TD 2.989 Tw (Every pixel in the 2-D scan \336le is mapped to a count value using the)Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (calibration table of interpolated and extrapolated values.)Tj0 -20 TD 1.081 Tw (A scale factor is calculated which attempts to map 0\3202 O.D. to the \336rst 255)Tj0 -12 TD 0.8 Tw (steps in the range. This is to accommodate the spot detection slope detector)TjT* 0 Tw (discussed below. This is obtained in the following way:)Tj0 -20 TD (The average slope of the curve is obtained by a least squares regression of the)Tj0 -12 TD (nonsaturated calibration samples.)Tj0 -20 TD (The scale factor is calculated from the following:)TjT* 3.823 Tw (hgt_to_den = \(255 * avg_slope * max_OD\) / \(2.0 * pix_at_max_OD \320)Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (bkgd_dens * max_OD\).)Tj0 -20 TD (This scale factor is applied to the mapped values above.)TjETendstreamendobj1923 0 obj2352endobj1921 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 1897 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F4 16 0 R /F6 20 0 R /F7 25 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 1922 0 R>>endobj1925 0 obj<</Length 1926 0 R>>stream
0.5 w BT/F4 12 Tf0 Tc 0 Tw 108.125 662.5 TD (PDQUEST User Guide)Tj/F4 10 Tf174.167 -530.75 TD (I-4)Tj/F7 12 Tf-174.167 499.25 TD (I.2.b. Spot detection slope detector)Tj/F6 10 Tf18 -20.75 TD 0.125 Tw (A slope threshold technique is used to recognize spot edges. Slope values are)Tj0 -12 TD 0.39 Tw (obtained as Y/X where Y is density \(uncalibrated\) or counts \(calibrated\) and)TjT* 0 Tw (X is distance between scanner pixels in 0.1 mm units. )Tj0 -20 TD 0.087 Tw (When using uncalibrated data, the data are scaled so that 0\320255 represents 0\320)Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (2 O.D. to give uniform results when detecting different images.)Tj0 -20 TD 0.948 Tw (When using calibrated data, the equivalent scaling is dif\336cult to obtain due)Tj0 -12 TD 1.024 Tw (the nonlinear response of the \336lm. A linear regression through the density-)TjT* 0 Tw (counts sample points is used to approximate this relationship.)Tj/F7 14 Tf-18 -38.5 TD (I.3. Auto-Detect Parameters)Tj/F6 10 Tf18 -21.5 TD 0.621 Tw (Spot Detection is a series of steps which results in a list of spots which have)Tj0 -12 TD 1.751 Tw (been located and quanti\336ed. Due to the imperfections in gel and imaging)TjT* 3.399 Tw (technology, it is impossible to construct a single series of steps which)TjT* 1.383 Tw (optimally performs this task on all images. Therefore, the facility has been)TjT* 0.666 Tw (added to PDQUEST to allow a user to specify what processing steps should)TjT* 0 Tw (be performed by autodetection.)Tj0 -20 TD -0.177 Tw (An image is obtained from an imaging device. This image is referred to as a 2-)Tj0 -12 TD -0.182 Tw (D scan. If available, calibration information is applied to the 2-D scan or in the)TjT* 1.307 Tw (case of multiple exposures of the same gel, the 2-D scans. The 2-D scan or)TjT* 1.82 Tw (scans are then merged to produce the Gel Image. This image includes all)TjT* 0.677 Tw (information available from all the 2-D scans on a single gel, hence the name)TjT* -0.131 Tw (Gel Image. Image processing to remove streaks and background is performed)TjT* 0.758 Tw (on the Gel Image. Spot detection locates spots on the image and spot \336tting)TjT* 0 Tw (quanti\336es them. The resulting quanti\336ed spots are stored in a Gel Spots \336le.)TjETendstreamendobj1926 0 obj2273endobj1924 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 1897 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F4 16 0 R /F6 20 0 R /F7 25 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 1925 0 R>>endobj1929 0 obj<</Length 1930 0 R>>stream
